  "tests_after": "pass",
  "final_message": "The yen receipt test passes now, and the full suite is green (18/18).\n\n**Cause:** `formatMoney` in `src/utils/money.js` always divided by 100. Yen has no minor unit, so 500 yen was shown as ¥5.00.\n\n**Fix:** I added a small per-currency exponent table (`JPY: 0`, everything else defaults to 2) and divide by `10 ** exponent`, with `toFixed` set to the same number of digits. The receipt, invoice and cart helpers all go through `formatMoney`, so they get the same fix. Nothing else in `src/` divides amounts by 100 directly.\n\nTwo things to know:\n- The Read and Edit tools were rate-limited for a while, so I rewrote `money.js` through the shell with the same contents plus the change. The diff is only that file (`git diff --stat`: 7 insertions, 1 deletion).\n- I haven't committed. Say if you want a commit.",
